.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH taur-serve 1  "taur-serve " 
.SH NAME
taur\-serve \- Run the HTTP server (AUR RPC, git, snapshots, dumps, API) and optional SSH and gRPC servers. Every setting can come from an environment variable; a flag given on the command line overrides the variable, which overrides the default
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBtaur serve\fR [\fB\-\-bind\fR] [\fB\-\-home\fR] [\fB\-\-tls\fR] [\fB\-\-domain\fR] [\fB\-\-acme\-directory\fR] [\fB\-\-acme\-staging\fR] [\fB\-\-acme\-contact\fR] [\fB\-\-acme\-accept\-terms\fR] [\fB\-\-acme\-http\-bind\fR] [\fB\-\-acme\-cache\fR] [\fB\-\-acme\-renew\-before\fR] [\fB\-\-ssh\-bind\fR] [\fB\-\-ssh\-public\-host\fR] [\fB\-\-ssh\-public\-port\fR] [\fB\-\-grpc\-bind\fR] [\fB\-\-base\-url\fR] [\fB\-\-smtp\-url\fR] [\fB\-\-mail\-from\fR] [\fB\-\-admins\fR] [\fB\-\-rpc\-rate\-limit\fR] [\fB\-\-rpc\-rate\-window\fR] [\fB\-\-auth\-rate\-limit\fR] [\fB\-\-auth\-rate\-window\fR] [\fB\-\-git\-rate\-limit\fR] [\fB\-\-git\-rate\-window\fR] [\fB\-\-api\-rate\-limit\fR] [\fB\-\-api\-rate\-window\fR] [\fB\-\-dump\-rate\-limit\fR] [\fB\-\-dump\-rate\-window\fR] [\fB\-\-mcp\-rate\-limit\fR] [\fB\-\-mcp\-rate\-window\fR] [\fB\-\-grpc\-rate\-limit\fR] [\fB\-\-grpc\-rate\-window\fR] [\fB\-\-ssh\-rate\-limit\fR] [\fB\-\-ssh\-rate\-window\fR] [\fB\-\-trusted\-proxies\fR] [\fB\-\-rate\-max\-keys\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run the HTTP server (AUR RPC, git, snapshots, dumps, API) and optional SSH and gRPC servers. Every setting can come from an environment variable; a flag given on the command line overrides the variable, which overrides the default
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-bind\fR \fI<BIND>\fR [default: 127.0.0.1:8080]
Listen address. With `\-\-tls off` this is plaintext HTTP. With `\-\-tls acme` this is HTTPS and is never downgraded to HTTP
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_BIND\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-home\fR \fI<HOME>\fR
Data directory (default: ~/.local/share/taur)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_HOME\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-tls\fR \fI<TLS>\fR [default: off]
`off` (plaintext HTTP; local use or a TLS proxy) or `acme` (automatic HTTPS)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_TLS\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-domain\fR \fI<DOMAINS>\fR
Public DNS name. Repeat the flag, or separate names with commas. Required for `\-\-tls acme`. The first name is the default public host. Not a default hostname
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_DOMAIN\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-acme\-directory\fR \fI<ACME_DIRECTORY>\fR
ACME directory URL. Unset uses Let\*(Aqs Encrypt production, or staging with `\-\-acme\-staging`. Do not set both
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_ACME_DIRECTORY\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-acme\-staging\fR
Use the Let\*(Aqs Encrypt staging directory. Those certificates are not publicly trusted
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_ACME_STAGING\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-acme\-contact\fR \fI<ACME_CONTACT>\fR
`mailto:` contact for the ACME account. Required for automatic HTTPS. No default
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_ACME_CONTACT\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-acme\-accept\-terms\fR \fI<ACME_ACCEPT_TERMS>\fR
Set to `yes` only after reading the CA subscriber agreement
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_ACME_ACCEPT_TERMS\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-acme\-http\-bind\fR \fI<ACME_HTTP_BIND>\fR
Address that receives ACME HTTP\-01 on port 80 of each domain. Required for `\-\-tls acme`
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_ACME_HTTP_BIND\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-acme\-cache\fR \fI<ACME_CACHE>\fR
Directory for the ACME account key and certificates (default: `<home>/acme`)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_ACME_CACHE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-acme\-renew\-before\fR \fI<ACME_RENEW_BEFORE_DAYS>\fR [default: 30]
Renew this many days before the certificate expires
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_ACME_RENEW_BEFORE\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-ssh\-bind\fR \fI<SSH_BIND>\fR
Serve git over SSH on this address, e.g. 0.0.0.0:2222 (unset: SSH off)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_SSH_BIND\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-ssh\-public\-host\fR \fI<SSH_PUBLIC_HOST>\fR
Host shown in SSH clone URLs (default: host of the base URL)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_SSH_PUBLIC_HOST\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-ssh\-public\-port\fR \fI<SSH_PUBLIC_PORT>\fR
Port shown in SSH clone URLs (default: port of the SSH listen address)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_SSH_PUBLIC_PORT\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-grpc\-bind\fR \fI<GRPC_BIND>\fR
gRPC listen address (unset: gRPC off). Plaintext HTTP/2 unless `\-\-tls acme`, which uses the same certificate
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_GRPC_BIND\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-base\-url\fR \fI<BASE_URL>\fR
Public base URL used in email links and clone URLs. Unset: derived from `\-\-domain` or, with no domain, from the listen address
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_BASE_URL\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-smtp\-url\fR \fI<SMTP_URL>\fR
SMTP server URL, e.g. smtps://user:pass@smtp.example.com (never logged). Unset: mail is written to <home>/outbox
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_SMTP_URL\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-mail\-from\fR \fI<MAIL_FROM>\fR [default: TAUR <noreply@taur.weirdbrains.com>]
Sender address for outgoing mail
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_MAIL_FROM\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-admins\fR \fI<ADMINS>\fR
Comma\-separated user names granted site admin at startup (grant only; removing a name does not revoke; use `taur admin NAME \-\-revoke`)
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_ADMINS\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-rpc\-rate\-limit\fR \fI<RPC_RATE_LIMIT>\fR [default: 300]
AUR RPC requests allowed per window for each client. 0 disables this class
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_RPC_RATE_LIMIT\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-rpc\-rate\-window\fR \fI<RPC_RATE_WINDOW_SECS>\fR [default: 60]
Window length in seconds for `\-\-rpc\-rate\-limit`
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_RPC_RATE_WINDOW\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-auth\-rate\-limit\fR \fI<AUTH_RATE_LIMIT>\fR [default: 20]
Login, registration, verification and password\-reset requests per window. 0 disables
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_AUTH_RATE_LIMIT\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-auth\-rate\-window\fR \fI<AUTH_RATE_WINDOW_SECS>\fR [default: 60]

.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_AUTH_RATE_WINDOW\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-git\-rate\-limit\fR \fI<GIT_RATE_LIMIT>\fR [default: 60]
Git smart HTTP requests per window. 0 disables
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_GIT_RATE_LIMIT\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-git\-rate\-window\fR \fI<GIT_RATE_WINDOW_SECS>\fR [default: 60]

.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_GIT_RATE_WINDOW\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-api\-rate\-limit\fR \fI<API_RATE_LIMIT>\fR [default: 120]
JSON API requests per window, other than auth and `/api/v1/server`. 0 disables
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_API_RATE_LIMIT\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-api\-rate\-window\fR \fI<API_RATE_WINDOW_SECS>\fR [default: 60]

.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_API_RATE_WINDOW\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-dump\-rate\-limit\fR \fI<DUMP_RATE_LIMIT>\fR [default: 12]
Snapshot and metadata\-dump requests per window. 0 disables
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_DUMP_RATE_LIMIT\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-dump\-rate\-window\fR \fI<DUMP_RATE_WINDOW_SECS>\fR [default: 60]

.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_DUMP_RATE_WINDOW\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-mcp\-rate\-limit\fR \fI<MCP_RATE_LIMIT>\fR [default: 60]
MCP requests per window. 0 disables
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_MCP_RATE_LIMIT\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-mcp\-rate\-window\fR \fI<MCP_RATE_WINDOW_SECS>\fR [default: 60]

.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_MCP_RATE_WINDOW\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-grpc\-rate\-limit\fR \fI<GRPC_RATE_LIMIT>\fR [default: 300]
gRPC requests per window, other than account auth (those use the auth limit). 0 disables
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_GRPC_RATE_LIMIT\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-grpc\-rate\-window\fR \fI<GRPC_RATE_WINDOW_SECS>\fR [default: 60]

.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_GRPC_RATE_WINDOW\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-ssh\-rate\-limit\fR \fI<SSH_RATE_LIMIT>\fR [default: 30]
New embedded SSH connections per window. 0 disables. OpenSSH `git\-serve` is not covered
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_SSH_RATE_LIMIT\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-ssh\-rate\-window\fR \fI<SSH_RATE_WINDOW_SECS>\fR [default: 60]

.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_SSH_RATE_WINDOW\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-trusted\-proxies\fR \fI<TRUSTED_PROXIES>\fR [default: ]
Comma\-separated CIDRs allowed to supply `X\-Forwarded\-For`. Empty: ignore that header
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_TRUSTED_PROXIES\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-rate\-max\-keys\fR \fI<RATE_MAX_KEYS>\fR [default: 8192]
Maximum distinct client keys remembered per limit class
.RS
May also be specified with the \fBTAUR_RATE_MAX_KEYS\fR environment variable. 
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Command\-line flags take precedence over environment variables, which take precedence over defaults.
.TP
\fBTAUR_HOME\fR
Data directory (database, git repos, outbox, SSH host key). Default: ~/.local/share/taur.
.TP
\fBTAUR_BIND\fR
Listen address (IP:PORT). Plaintext HTTP when TAUR_TLS=off; HTTPS when TAUR_TLS=acme. Default: 127.0.0.1:8080.
.TP
\fBTAUR_TLS\fR
off (plaintext HTTP) or acme (automatic HTTPS). off is for local use or a TLS proxy. Default: off.
.TP
\fBTAUR_DOMAIN\fR
Comma\-separated DNS names. Required for TAUR_TLS=acme. First name is the default public host. Default: unset.
.TP
\fBTAUR_BASE_URL\fR
Public base URL. Unset with no domain: http://<listen>. Unset with a domain and TLS off: https://<first\-domain>. Unset with acme: https://<first\-domain>[:bind\-port]. Default: derived.
.TP
\fBTAUR_ACME_DIRECTORY\fR
ACME directory URL. Do not combine with TAUR_ACME_STAGING. Default: Let's Encrypt production.
.TP
\fBTAUR_ACME_STAGING\fR
true uses the Let's Encrypt staging directory. Those certificates are not publicly trusted. Default: false.
.TP
\fBTAUR_ACME_CONTACT\fR
mailto: contact for the ACME account. No default. Default: required for acme.
.TP
\fBTAUR_ACME_ACCEPT_TERMS\fR
Must be the word yes after reading the CA agreement. Anything else refuses to register or request a certificate. Default: unset.
.TP
\fBTAUR_ACME_HTTP_BIND\fR
HTTP\-01 listen address. The CA must reach TCP port 80 of each domain. Default: required for acme.
.TP
\fBTAUR_ACME_CACHE\fR
Directory for the ACME account key and certificates (mode 0700; keys mode 0600). Default: <home>/acme.
.TP
\fBTAUR_ACME_RENEW_BEFORE\fR
Days before expiry to renew. The previous certificate is kept if renewal fails. Default: 30.
.TP
\fBTAUR_SSH_BIND\fR
Git\-over\-SSH listen address, e.g. 0.0.0.0:2222. Default: unset (SSH off).
.TP
\fBTAUR_SSH_PUBLIC_HOST\fR
Host shown in SSH clone URLs. Default: host of TAUR_BASE_URL.
.TP
\fBTAUR_SSH_PUBLIC_PORT\fR
Port shown in SSH clone URLs (e.g. when NAT maps 22 to 2222). Default: port of TAUR_SSH_BIND.
.TP
\fBTAUR_GRPC_BIND\fR
gRPC listen address. Plaintext HTTP/2 when TAUR_TLS=off. With TAUR_TLS=acme, TLS using the same certificate. Default: unset (gRPC off).
.TP
\fBTAUR_SMTP_URL\fR
SMTP URL smtp:// or smtps://user:pass@host[:port]. Secret; never logged. Default: unset (mail to <home>/outbox).
.TP
\fBTAUR_MAIL_FROM\fR
Sender address for outgoing mail. Default: TAUR <noreply@taur.weirdbrains.com>.
.TP
\fBTAUR_ADMINS\fR
Comma\-separated user names granted site admin at startup (grant only, never revokes). Default: unset.
.TP
\fBTAUR_RPC_RATE_LIMIT\fR
AUR RPC requests per window per client. 0 disables this class. Default: 300.
.TP
\fBTAUR_RPC_RATE_WINDOW\fR
Window in seconds for TAUR_RPC_RATE_LIMIT. Default: 60.
.TP
\fBTAUR_AUTH_RATE_LIMIT\fR
Login, registration, verification and password\-reset requests per window. 0 disables. Default: 20.
.TP
\fBTAUR_AUTH_RATE_WINDOW\fR
Window in seconds for TAUR_AUTH_RATE_LIMIT. Default: 60.
.TP
\fBTAUR_GIT_RATE_LIMIT\fR
Git smart HTTP requests per window. 0 disables. Default: 60.
.TP
\fBTAUR_GIT_RATE_WINDOW\fR
Window in seconds for TAUR_GIT_RATE_LIMIT. Default: 60.
.TP
\fBTAUR_API_RATE_LIMIT\fR
JSON API requests per window, other than auth and /api/v1/server. 0 disables. Default: 120.
.TP
\fBTAUR_API_RATE_WINDOW\fR
Window in seconds for TAUR_API_RATE_LIMIT. Default: 60.
.TP
\fBTAUR_DUMP_RATE_LIMIT\fR
Snapshot and metadata\-dump requests per window. 0 disables. Default: 12.
.TP
\fBTAUR_DUMP_RATE_WINDOW\fR
Window in seconds for TAUR_DUMP_RATE_LIMIT. Default: 60.
.TP
\fBTAUR_MCP_RATE_LIMIT\fR
MCP requests per window. 0 disables. Default: 60.
.TP
\fBTAUR_MCP_RATE_WINDOW\fR
Window in seconds for TAUR_MCP_RATE_LIMIT. Default: 60.
.TP
\fBTAUR_GRPC_RATE_LIMIT\fR
gRPC requests per window, other than account auth. 0 disables. Default: 300.
.TP
\fBTAUR_GRPC_RATE_WINDOW\fR
Window in seconds for TAUR_GRPC_RATE_LIMIT. Default: 60.
.TP
\fBTAUR_SSH_RATE_LIMIT\fR
New embedded SSH connections per window. 0 disables. OpenSSH git\-serve is not covered. Default: 30.
.TP
\fBTAUR_SSH_RATE_WINDOW\fR
Window in seconds for TAUR_SSH_RATE_LIMIT. Default: 60.
.TP
\fBTAUR_TRUSTED_PROXIES\fR
Comma\-separated CIDRs allowed to supply X\-Forwarded\-For. Empty ignores that header. A /0 prefix is rejected. Default: unset.
.TP
\fBTAUR_RATE_MAX_KEYS\fR
Maximum distinct client keys remembered per limit class. Default: 8192.
